// startingPoint.js — the Fall 2026 starting point of Black Belt testing, as JavaScript.
// Why it exists: migration 0016 seeds ONE row in public.bb_starting_point (section 11n): the
// Fall 2026 schedule, plans, amounts, due dates and Kukkiwon fees ("schedule"), and the Fall 2026
// requirements sheet ("requirements"). The very first Add cycle is filled in from it. The preview
// database (mockBlackBelt.js) starts from exactly the same values, so preview shows what the real
// database will show. Nobody in the app can read the real row (it is never granted); only
// bb_cycle_defaults() hands its schedule to Add cycle.
//
// The two objects below are the two $bbjson$ blocks of supabase/migrations/0016_black_belt.sql,
// copied word for word, and SEED_WAIVER_BODY is its $bbwaiver$ text (the PLACEHOLDER waiver,
// version 2026-1). checks.mjs reads the SQL file and FAILS if they ever differ, so a change to the
// seed must be made in both places.
// Money is in whole cents (87000 = $870). Dates are Massachusetts school dates 'YYYY-MM-DD'.
// "to_confirm": true marks numbers still to confirm with Master Jeong (the seed review, CP1).
//
// Imported only by the preview database and checks.mjs (never by the live build's screens).

// The name Add cycle shows as "Filled in from …" for the starting point (bb_cycle_defaults).
export const STARTING_POINT_NAME = 'Fall 2026 starting point';

// The seeded waiver version: a placeholder. Registration can't open while it is current
// (bb_set_registration answers waiver_needed, contract 0016 OI-1).
export const SEED_WAIVER_VERSION_NAME = '2026-1';
export const SEED_WAIVER_BODY = "PLACEHOLDER — replace with the school's waiver before opening registration.\n\nBlack Belt testing agreement (the points of the old registration page, kept here only until the school's own waiver text is saved on Rubric and prices):\n\n1. Every subject must be passed. A subject that is not passed is made up at a later testing.\n2. Testing fees are non-refundable. If the candidate does not pass, the fees are applied to the next test.\n3. I understand that Taekwondo training and testing are physical activities that carry a risk of injury, and I accept that risk.\n4. I release Jae H. Jeong's U.S. Taekwondo Center, its owners, instructors and staff from claims for injuries that happen during training or testing.\n\nBy signing below I agree to the above.";

